{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04M8", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$[U/_{\\!p}R]$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathit{Isom}(x, y)$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathit{Isom}(x', y')$", "MATH_0004": "$[U/_{\\!p}R]$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\mathit{Isom}(x', y') = S' \\times_{(y', x'), U \\times_S U} R\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-quotient-stack}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-quotient-stack-arrows}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fb9bad6bba90a6611dd3595eb2a1ebad0d088bd9200aa11d165183258b89b4ec", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:820f3a0d0a05503c1091f94a8ec86e4fc71d19eb29f4da3d434b2458089b4323", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be the category fibred in groupoids associated to\nthe presheaf in groupoids (<REF_0001>) as in the proof of\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nBy construction the sheaf <MATH_0002> is the sheaf associated\nto the presheaf <MATH_0003>. On the other hand, by definition\nof morphisms in <MATH_0004> we have\n<MATH_0005>\nand the right hand side is an algebraic space, therefore a sheaf.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0a8cd6bfeb8921e7215d41f74fc729197d6b4749004acb8109403aa53dafd35c", "unit_id": "tag:044V:proof"}
{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04M8", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$B \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0003": "$\\pi : \\mathcal{S}_U \\to [U/R]$", "MATH_0004": "$2$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{S}_R \\ar[r]_s \\ar[d]_t & \\mathcal{S}_U \\ar[d]^\\pi \\\\\n\\mathcal{S}_U \\ar[r]^-\\pi & [U/R]\n}\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$2$", "MATH_0007": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-quotient-stack-arrows}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-quotient-stack-2-arrow}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-quotient-stack-2-cartesian}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ff671ce92306d41f3e3dabb558d29104eacaa0918a115dd1877ffbe4b886a0a2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a9a8a6c9db8c9bd9fbc7c917eadf60c11c3a15d422d211d3a879a1081ea53658", "source_text": "Assume <MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002>, and <MATH_0003>\nare as in\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nThe <MATH_0004>-commutative square\n<MATH_0005>\nof\nLemma <REF_0002>\nis a <MATH_0006>-fibre product of stacks in groupoids of <MATH_0007>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:626e2e90a703f76658ee32d4ad3c2bc17736294daa282f096ed7eeb397b4523b", "unit_id": "tag:04M9:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04M8", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\mathcal{S}_R \\longrightarrow \\mathcal{S}_U \\times_{[U/R]} \\mathcal{S}_U\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$r : T \\to R$", "MATH_0003": "$(T, t(r), s(r), \\alpha(r))$", "MATH_0004": "$2$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-lemma-2-product-stacks-in-groupoids}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{categories-lemma-2-product-categories-over-C}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-quotient-stack-morphisms}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-cartesian-square-of-morphism}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b9cd8280a9e3b37613354dba99fb182fe391b4d6c9f67fada7373c61aa7d2c07", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:601a801b658518472566a2f5375994e802b237ecb5d9a3fa5d601e8b8fbdc9a9", "source_text": "According to\nStacks, Lemma <REF_0001>\nthe lemma makes sense. It also tells us that we have to show that\nthe functor\n<MATH_0001>\nwhich maps <MATH_0002> to <MATH_0003> is an equivalence,\nwhere the right hand side is the <MATH_0004>-fibre product as described in\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nThis is, after spelling out the definitions, exactly the content of\nLemma <REF_0003>. (Alternative proof: Work out\nthe meaning of\nLemma <REF_0004>\nin this situation will give you the result also.)\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ec7592312dc3452bc6e29a02e601f5311b0e0802f2e20e81571e539c430a5e98", "unit_id": "tag:04M9:proof"}
